body:
🟡 On the home page, `VaultCard` renders no kind label or sync-status dot for external-store vaults, even though `GET /v1/vaults` now emits `credential_store` per item (handle_vaults.go:652,675). The `Vault` interface at VaultsListTab.tsx:13-21 was not extended with `credential_store`, so the field is silently dropped on the client. `SyncStatusDot` was added to `web/src/components/shared.tsx` in this PR specifically for this purpose but has zero callers across the codebase — dead code as shipped. The PR description explicitly promises "Web UI: vault cards show a status pill." Fix: extend the Vault interface with the `CredentialStoreInfo` shape already defined in router.tsx, and render `SyncStatusDot` + kind label in the card header.

<details>
<summary>Extended reasoning...</summary>

## What the bug is

The server-side `handleVaultList` (internal/server/handle_vaults.go:600-678) now emits a per-vault `credential_store: { kind, last_sync_status, last_synced_at }` field for every external-store vault, populated via the new `credStoreFor` helper. The matching CLI surface (`cmd/vaults.go`) was extended to render a `STORE` column, and the vault-detail surfaces (`SettingsTab.tsx` Settings panel, `CredentialsTab.tsx` read-only banner, `ProposalsTab.tsx` banner) all consume the field correctly.

The home-page `VaultCard` consumer at `web/src/pages/home/VaultsListTab.tsx` does not. Its `Vault` interface (lines 13-21) declares only `{id, name, role, membership, is_default?, created_at, pending_proposals}` — no `credential_store` member. The PR did not touch this interface. `encoding/json`-style `JSON.parse` drops the unknown field, and `VaultCard` (lines 175-292) renders no badge/pill/dot for external-store vaults: the header has Join button | pending-proposals badge | delete button, and the footer row has only `timeAgo(vault.created_at)` + `vault.role`. There is no reference to `credential_store` anywhere in this file outside the new `CreateVaultButton` form.

## Why this is the asymmetric one

The PR added `SyncStatusDot` to `web/src/components/shared.tsx` in this same change. A repo-wide grep for `SyncStatusDot` returns exactly one file — the definition itself. Zero callers. The component was clearly written for the home-page `VaultCard` (the only surface that currently lacks a sync-status indicator) but the wiring was never finished.

The asymmetry is striking. Every other surface added by this PR wires `credential_store` correctly:
- `cmd/vaults.go:191` (`vault list`) — added a `STORE` column.
- `web/src/pages/vault/SettingsTab.tsx` — renders `CredentialStoreSection` with kind + sync status + last-synced timestamp.
- `web/src/pages/vault/CredentialsTab.tsx` — renders the read-only `InfoBanner` and manual-sync button.
- `web/src/pages/vault/ProposalsTab.tsx` — renders the read-only banner.
- `web/src/pages/home/VaultsListTab.tsx` — nothing.

The PR description explicitly promises this surface under "Surface area > Web UI": *"vault cards show a status pill"*. That promise is not met on the home page.

## Step-by-step proof

1. Operator deploys with `INFISICAL_URL` set and creates two vaults: `builtin-vault` (no `--credential-store`) and `ext-vault` (`--credential-store=infisical`).
2. Operator opens the home page; the browser issues `GET /v1/vaults`.
3. `handleVaultList` builds `csByVault` from `ListVaultCredentialStores`, attaches `credential_store: {kind: "infisical", last_sync_status: "ok", last_synced_at: ...}` to the `ext-vault` item.
4. The browser receives both items; `JSON.parse` succeeds; the unknown `credential_store` field on `ext-vault` is preserved on the parsed object **but** the TypeScript `Vault` interface (lines 13-21) does not declare it, so subsequent consumers see no field.
5. `VaultCard` for `ext-vault` and `VaultCard` for `builtin-vault` render identically: vault name, time-ago, role. Indistinguishable.

## Impact

No security or correctness impact — the mutation gate `assertBuiltinCredentialStore` at `internal/server/server.go:578` correctly returns `409 external_credential_store` regardless of UI state, and the detail-page surfaces all render the credential-store info once the user clicks through. The cost is pure discoverability: an operator scanning the home page cannot tell which vaults are external-backed without clicking into each one.

Worth filing because (a) the PR description explicitly promises this surface and ships a dead component intended for it, (b) the fix is small (~5 lines: extend the interface with the `CredentialStoreInfo` shape already exported from `router.tsx`, then render `SyncStatusDot` + kind label in the card header), and (c) the gap is the only asymmetric surface in an otherwise consistently-wired feature.

## How to fix

```tsx
// VaultsListTab.tsx, near the top
import type { AuthContext, CredentialStoreInfo } from "../../router";
import { SyncStatusDot } from "../../components/shared";

interface Vault {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  role: string;
  membership: "explicit" | "implicit";
  is_default?: boolean;
  created_at: string;
  pending_proposals: number;
  credential_store?: CredentialStoreInfo;
}
```

Then in `VaultCard`’s header, render the store indicator alongside the existing children:

```tsx
{vault.credential_store && (
  <span className="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs bg-surface-raised text-text-muted border border-border">
    <SyncStatusDot status={vault.credential_store.last_sync_status} />
    {vault.credential_store.kind}
  </span>
)}
```

That wires the already-exported `SyncStatusDot` into its intended caller and brings the home-page card into symmetry with the CLI `STORE` column and the detail-page surfaces.

</details>

